{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Son of the Canaanite woman.</b> This verse testifies that the wives of the tribes were Egyptian, Edomite, Midianite, and he mentioned this one alone because Shimon acted improperly in taking a Canaanite woman, and on this account he mentioned the death of Er and Onan, because they were sons of a Canaanite woman. Another interpretation: the reason he mentioned Er and Onan here, even though they died before the descent to Egypt, is because through Judah they descended to Egypt — for had he wished to protest the sale of Joseph, they would have listened to him. HaShem said: you did not spare your father's grief; by your life, at the time your father is rejoicing, the death of your sons shall be recalled, so as to pain you."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:47.215061847Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}